    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83366" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῐτῠο-κάμπτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pinebender</i>, epith. of Sinis, who killed
			travellers by tying them between two pine-trees bent down so as
			nearly to meet, and then let go again, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.1.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
				3.16.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				8
			</span></i> :—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῐτῠκάμπτης</span></b> , prob. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παλικάμπῃ</span> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.107
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Lucill.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
